# Agent Tab — environment variables
# Copy to .env for local development. Do not commit .env.

# --- Database ---
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# --- ChainCash sidecar ---
SIDECAR_URL="http://localhost:8081"

# --- NextAuth (production envelope foundation) ---
# Required in all environments.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-random-32-byte-secret"

# --- Email magic-link sign-in ---
# In DEV: leave EMAIL_SERVER unset. The login flow short-circuits and prints
# the magic link to the Next.js dev server terminal. Copy/paste into the
# browser to complete sign-in. No SMTP service required.
#
# In PRODUCTION: set EMAIL_SERVER to a real SMTP connection string, e.g.:
#   EMAIL_SERVER="smtp://user:pass@smtp.example.com:587"
# and EMAIL_FROM to a verified sender address.
# EMAIL_SERVER=""
EMAIL_FROM="noreply@agent-credit.local"

# --- Default operator (production envelope, slice 2) ---
# Email used by scripts/backfill-default-operator.ts to upsert the operator
# User and claim ownership of existing Customer rows whose ownerUserId is null.
#
# In DEV: leave unset to use the dev fallback "operator@agent-credit.local".
# In PRODUCTION: required. The backfill script fails closed if unset.
#
# Once set, do not change without re-running the backfill — changing the
# email would create a second operator and leave existing customers owned
# by the original.
# DEFAULT_OPERATOR_EMAIL=""

# --- Agent API key pepper (production envelope, slice 8A) ---
# Server-side secret used to compute HMAC-SHA256(pepper, rawApiKey) for
# AgentIdentity.apiKeyHash. /api/proxy compares the submitted x-agent-api-key
# against the stored hash; the pepper raises the cost of a DB-leak attack
# (an attacker with the DB still needs the pepper to verify candidate keys).
#
# In DEV: leave unset to use a built-in dev fallback. A one-time warning is
# logged when first used. Do NOT rely on the dev fallback in production.
#
# In PRODUCTION: required. The hash helper throws if AGENT_API_KEY_PEPPER is
# missing or empty when NODE_ENV=production. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Stability: this value MUST be stable across deployments. Changing it
# invalidates every stored apiKeyHash — every agent's existing key would
# stop authenticating. Slice 8A does not include a pepper-rotation strategy;
# pick a strong value at first prod deploy and keep it.
# AGENT_API_KEY_PEPPER=""
